---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const canonical = new URL('/terms/', Astro.site).href;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions — RealWordCounter"
  description="Terms and conditions for using RealWordCounter.com — free word counter and writing tools. Please read before using the site."
  canonical={canonical}
  ogImage="og-home.png"
>

  <div class="container" style="padding-top:var(--space-8);padding-bottom:var(--space-4)">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb-sep">›</span>
      <span class="breadcrumb-current">Terms and Conditions</span>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <div class="container policy-wrap">
    <div class="policy-header">
      <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="policy-meta">Last updated: June 2025 · Effective immediately</p>
      <p class="policy-intro">
        Please read these terms carefully before using RealWordCounter.com. By accessing or
        using any part of this website, you agree to be bound by these terms.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="policy-body">

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing and using RealWordCounter.com ("the Site", "we", "our"), you accept and
          agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions and our
          <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree to these terms,
          please do not use the Site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>2. Description of Service</h2>
        <p>
          RealWordCounter provides free, browser-based writing tools including a word counter,
          character counter, readability checker, platform limits checker, UPSC exam presets,
          text case converter, and related utilities. All processing happens locally in your
          browser — no text is transmitted to our servers.
        </p>
        <p>
          The service is provided free of charge and "as is." We reserve the right to modify,
          suspend, or discontinue any part of the service at any time without prior notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>3. Use of the Site</h2>
        <p>You agree to use the Site only for lawful purposes. You must not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the Site in any way that violates applicable local, national, or international law or regulation</li>
          <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the Site or its related systems</li>
          <li>Use automated scripts, bots, or scrapers to access the Site in a manner that could overload or damage our infrastructure</li>
          <li>Reproduce, duplicate, copy, or resell any part of the Site in a way that competes with our service without written permission</li>
          <li>Transmit any unsolicited or unauthorised advertising or promotional material</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          The Site and its original content (excluding content you input into the tools),
          features, and functionality are owned by RealWordCounter and are protected by
          applicable intellectual property laws.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Your content remains yours.</strong> Any text you type or paste into our
          tools is your own intellectual property. We make no claim to it, and as stated
          in our Privacy Policy, we never store or access it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>5. Accuracy of Information</h2>
        <p>
          Our tools aim to provide accurate counts and analysis. However, word count, readability
          scores, and character counts may vary slightly from other tools depending on how words
          and whitespace are defined. We do not warrant that the results are perfectly accurate
          for every use case.
        </p>
        <p>
          UPSC exam word limits, platform character limits, and other reference data are based on
          publicly available information and may change. Always verify critical limits from the
          official source before submitting academic or professional work.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>6. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          THE SITE IS PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" BASIS WITHOUT ANY WARRANTIES
          OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF
          MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not warrant that the Site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of viruses
          or other harmful components. You assume full responsibility for your use of the Site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, RealWordCounter shall not be liable for any
          indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use
          of or inability to use the Site, even if we have been advised of the possibility of
          such damages.
        </p>
        <p>
          This includes, but is not limited to, loss of data, loss of profit, or any damages
          resulting from reliance on word counts, readability scores, or any other output of
          our tools for academic, professional, or commercial purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>8. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p>
          The Site may contain links to third-party websites. These links are provided for
          convenience only. We have no control over the content of those sites and accept no
          responsibility for them or for any loss or damage that may arise from your use of them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India.
          Any disputes arising from these Terms or your use of the Site shall be subject to the
          exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of India.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>10. Changes to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to update these Terms at any time. The "Last updated" date at the
          top of this page reflects the most recent revision. Continued use of the Site after
          changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Reach us via the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
          We aim to respond within 48 hours on weekdays.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-wrap {
    max-width: 800px;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }

  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  .policy-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy-meta {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-mute);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-intro {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .policy-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-body);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy-section ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy-section li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-body);
  }

  .policy-section a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .policy-section a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
